-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Scope and third-party materials
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The MIT text above covers original CreditICL code and documentation. It does not
relicense datasets, third-party code, model weights or adapted model derivatives.
Their own notices and terms continue to apply.

Datasets
    Credit datasets are outside Git and have source-specific terms, including
    proprietary/anonymised sources. They are not distributed under this licence.
    The registry records known provenance; consult each source before reuse or
    redistribution. The pinned OpenML OOD inventory does not replace those terms.

Code and references
    src/models/nanotabiclv2.py retains its NanoTabICL attribution and MIT notice.
    It is a legacy diagnostic fallback, not the production model.
    Production uses the pinned upstream tabicl package and the TabPFN package;
    original credit-specific mechanisms and integration code live in this repo.
    src/data/dataset_preprocessing.py and dataset_registry.py originate from the
    sibling TabPFNCredit project by the same author/institution.
    Other dependencies retain their distributed licences and notices.
    tfm-library/ and vsc-library/ are separate pinned repositories; this licence
    does not cover their papers, code snapshots or other third-party contents.

Model weights
    Released and trained weights remain outside Git on VSC. TabPFN-3 is used for
    both reference evaluation and continued pretraining/constrained adaptation.
    Its model licence applies to the weights and adapted derivatives:
    https://huggingface.co/Prior-Labs/tabpfn_3/blob/main/LICENSE
    This project does not grant MIT rights over those artifacts.
    Released TabICLv2 assets likewise retain their upstream terms and notices.
    Prepare required weights before cluster computation; jobs do not perform
    interactive authentication or download missing models.

Citation
    CITATION.cff identifies the CreditICL software. Record the exact commit and
    cite relevant TabICLv2, TabPFN-3, data-source and methodological references
    separately. A software citation is not a claim of a published project paper.
